  "$schema": "https://aka.ms/codetour-schema",
  "title": "2: Create a database connection",
  "nextTour": "3: Bulk import users to a database connection",
  "steps": [
    {
      "file": "",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Test the default Auth0 database connection",
      "description": "## Test the default Auth0 database connection\n\nAuth0 provides database connections to authenticate users with an email/username and password. These credentials are securely stored in the Auth0 user store or in your own database. A default database connection is set up for you when your tenant was created.\n\nIn this exercise, you will explore the settings for the default database connection, and see what happens if an application has no connection enabled for it.\n\n1. In your tenant, select **Authentication** > **Database**. \n    >The available databae connections are displayed. You should see **Username-Password-Authentication**, which is available by default. This database stores accounts that are created by users or migrated in. Social connections will NOT appear here.\n      \n1. Select **Username-Password-Authentication** to open its settings.     \n     >In Settings, you can require usernames, disable signups, and import users from a legacy store (trickle migration).  \n      \n1. Select the **Authentication Methods** tab and select the button to configure the Password policy.\n    >Here you can customize your specific password policy, including password strength, history, a dictionary of forbidden passwords, and forbidding the use of personal data in passwords.  \n\n      \n1. Select the **Custom Database** tab. \n    >If you have an enterprise account you can enable a Custom Database connection to link to your own MySql, Mongo, SQL Server, etc. database. Here you would also set up your Database Actions scripts for user lifecycle operations:\n    \n    - Login\n    - Create\n    - Verify\n    - Change password\n    - Get user\n    - Delete  \n          \n    However, as you are signed up for a free Auth0 account, this feature will be disabled unless you upgrade to an Enterprise plan.   \n\n1. Select the **Applications** tab, then toggle switch next to the **Lab: Web App** to the off position.  \n\n1. Your app should still be running from the last time we launched it. Select [this link](command:auth0.lab.openEndpointByName?[\"Lab: Web App\"]) to open it in your browser.\n    - If it isn't still running, select [this link](command:workbench.action.debug.start) to start it up again.\n1. Select the log in link in the top right corner.\n    >Note that your login screen now only has sign-in with social connections, as you have disabled the database connection for this application. As this change was made in the tenant, and didn't require changes to application code, there was no need to rebuild the application.  \n1. Back in your tenant, re-enable the Username-Password-Authentication connection for **Lab: Web App** by switching the toggle button to the on position.\n  \n1. Select [this button](command:auth0.lab.openEndpointByName?[\"Lab: Web App\"]) to open your web app up again and click the login link. (You can also just refresh the page if you already have it open.)\n    >Username and password authentication is restored!  "
    },
    {
      "file": "",
      "line": 1,
      "title": "Create a new Auth0 database connection",
      "description": "## Create a new Auth0 database connection\n\nWe're going to import some user accounts into Auth0 - but before we do, let's create a new database connection for them. \n\n1. Go to **Authentication** > **Database**, and select **Create DB Connection**.\n      \n1. Enter **Contoso-Users** as the name for this database connection.\n\n1. Toggle on **Email Address** as an identifier.\n\n1. Select the **Create** button.\n    \n1. Select the **Applications** tab and enable this new connection for the  Lab: Web App application.  \n      \n1. Go to **Applications** > **Applications** and select **Lab: Web App**\n\n1. Select the **Connections** \n    Note this application is using two database connections:\n    - Username-Password-Authentication \n    - Contoso-Users\n    \n1. Disable the **Username-Password-Authentication** connection for the application by toggling it off.   \n    >This will ensure that only the users we're adding into the new database connection are able to log in. Next, we'll sign up using this new connection.\n"
    },
    {
      "title": "Sign up using the Contoso-Users connection",
      "description": "## Sign up using the Contoso-Users connection\n\n1. The app should still be running from the last time we launched it. Select [this link](command:auth0.lab.openEndpointByName?[\"Lab: Web App\"]) to open it in your browser.\n        -  If it isn't still running, select [this link](command:workbench.action.debug.start) to start it up again.\n1. Select the login link in the app\n        >The login screen is displayed because you have at least one connection enabled (The new Contoso database). But, there is no indication to the user that anything has changed.  \n1. Select the **Sign up** link and enter an email address that you have access to, along with a unique password for this new account. \n        - Use good password hygiene: Don’t use an existing password!\n        - **DO NOT** use social login. Instead, log in using a username and password.   \n        - If you've completed other labs and used a Gmail alias, you will want to increment the alias (+auth0labs2 for example) in order to sign up as a new unique user -- as you will need to receive the verification email. You may also just use any email address you have not used before and have access to. \n        \n1. From the Auth0 Dashboard, go to **User Management** > **Users**.  \n    >Note that you have a user with your email address and it is stored in the **Contoso-Users** database connection you created. \n        \n1. Go to **Applications** > **Applications** > **Lab: Web App** > **Connections** and re-enable the **Username-Password-Authentication** connection.\n\n\nWith the new database in place and enabled, we're ready to add some users."
    }
  ]
}
